<h2>What a Party Says</h2>

<p>At the April 30, 2024 Burke County work session, a presenter from a building company is recorded as saying that "Phase I of the project would begin in 2025 if approved." This is a statement by a party, as the county minutes print it.</p>

<p>The Governor's release of December 5, 2024 says: "The City of Waynesboro was awarded $2,496,190 in OneGeorgia funds to construct street, drainage, water, and sewer infrastructure that will allow for the construction of 51 new, housing units in St. George Crossing. The development is on a 190-acre tract." The release names the City as recipient and does not name the developer. It is the state's own description of the project.</p>

<p>The June 15, 2026 draft minutes state that "Abebe Ventures, LLC, the developer, will be responsible for all project costs exceeding the grant award and City contribution." The agreement's own text says: "The Developer will be responsible for any additional costs that exceed the grant award." The agreement copy is unsigned.</p>

<h2>Open Questions</h2>

<div class="fact-grid">
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>How did the Waynesboro council vote on items 5 and 6 on September 21, 2026? The minutes are not posted, so the vote on Resolution 2026-09-01 is not confirmed.</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>Which company was the applicant for the planned unit development on April 15, 2024? The minutes print "St. George Ventures LLC"; the 2026 agreement prints "Abebe Ventures, LLC". The records read do not state how the two names relate.</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>What did the council decide on the St. George Crossing zoning, regulating plan or ordinance, and when? The source did not find the council's zoning approval, any annexation, the grant application resolution, or any item on the December 2024 award, and lists no council records for 2023 or 2024.</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>What changes were requested at the September 23, 2025 Planning Commission meeting, and what did the planner present at the next meeting? The later meeting is not online.</p>
</div>

<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>On September 23, 2025 the Planning Commission minutes say of the project's regulating plan and ordinance: "Changes requested." No later approval of that plan was found in the records read. On June 15, 2026 the council approved the infrastructure agreement. <strong>Were the project's plans approved before the city signed?</strong></p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>The June 15, 2026 minutes read for this page are marked draft. Were they approved as written, and where are the approved minutes posted?</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>Were any conditions attached to the Atlanta rezoning as adopted? The adopted district carries no "conditional" suffix and the printout lists no conditions; the signed ordinance would confirm.</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>The council file page and the ordinance printout describe the June 15, 2026 Atlanta vote differently (roll call, consent vote), both 14 to 0. Which procedure was used?</p>
</div>
</div>

